  "description": "CUTWIZ crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H90 Dy4 F6 N12 O16. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.566-3.862 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.18-112.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C116 H90 Dy4 F6 N12 O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
